<%
// locals: sections ([{ title, items: [{ label, permId, description,
// checked, subpages: [...] }] }]) - see utils/portalPageCatalog.js's
// own buildSections, which is what every caller uses to build this.
//
// A real request: "the check boxes should all be in a single aligned
// column with the first word of the description lined up with its
// check box. The first word in each description should also start in
// its own clean column." Every page AND every one of its own subpages
// is flattened into this ONE .permission-checkbox-grid per section -
// not one grid per page - so nothing has to re-align between a page's
// own row and its own subpages' rows. Each .checkbox-option below is
// `display: contents` (public/css/styles.css), so its own <input> and
// two <span>s become the actual grid cells (column 1 / 2 / 3) rather
// than the label itself being one cell - every row's checkbox, marker,
// and text land in those same three columns regardless of text length
// or how deep a subpage list runs.
//
// A later real request: "the check boxes should show the actual
// description, not just a hover tooltip" - column 3 below is each
// permission's own full description (item.description/sp.description,
// e.g. "Manage the Members page's Approvals tab." on Admin Positions,
// or "View the Events page from Parent Portal." on Portal Permissions
// - the SAME underlying permissions.description column, worded
// differently per screen because of which `portal` each row's own
// permission belongs to, not two different fields) - the short catalog
// label (item.label) is no longer the visible row text at all, it only
// ever fed the description-as-tooltip this replaces. A permission
// whose description is ever missing falls back to its own label rather
// than rendering a blank row.
//
// A further real request: "Signify that its a subpage under a page by
// creating row lines to separate sections, bullet points for the main
// pages and dash lines for subpages." .permission-marker (column 2,
// between the checkbox and the description text) holds a plain bullet
// for every top-level page row and a dash for every one of its own
// subpage rows - its own fixed-width column (not just prefixed onto
// the description text itself) is what keeps column 3's own text
// starting at the exact same x position on EVERY row, main page or
// subpage alike, bullet/dash included - the literal "first word of the
// description... in its own clean column" requirement above still
// holds with these markers in play, not just without them.
// .permission-group-divider (a plain, non-.checkbox-option block
// spanning every column) is inserted after each top-level page's own
// complete group - the page's own row (or heading) plus every one of
// its own subpages - so a long list reads as separated sections instead
// of one undifferentiated wall of rows; the very last group in a
// section gets no trailing divider.
//
// A page with no permission of its own (key: null in the catalog - e.g.
// Parent Portal's "Co-op Classes," whose bare URL is identical to its
// own first subpage) renders as a plain, non-interactive group heading
// (.permission-group-label, spanning every column) instead of a
// checkbox - still prefixed with the same bullet every real top-level
// checkbox row gets, since it's still a main-page-level entry in this
// list, just one with no checkbox of its own to hang a marker column
// off of. Its own subpages (indented via .permission-subpage) are still
// real, independent checkboxes.
%>
<% (sections || []).forEach(function(section) { %>
  <% if (section.items && section.items.length) { %>
    <div class="permission-section">
      <p class="permission-section-title"><%= section.title %></p>
      <div class="permission-checkbox-grid">
        <% section.items.forEach(function(item, itemIndex) { %>
          <% if (item.permId) { %>
            <label class="checkbox-option">
              <input type="checkbox" name="permissionIds" value="<%= item.permId %>" <%= item.checked ? 'checked' : '' %> />
              <span class="permission-marker" aria-hidden="true">&bull;</span>
              <span class="permission-text"><%= item.description || item.label %></span>
            </label>
          <% } else { %>
            <span class="permission-group-label">&bull; <%= item.label %></span>
          <% } %>
          <% (item.subpages || []).forEach(function(sp) { %>
            <label class="checkbox-option permission-subpage">
              <input type="checkbox" name="permissionIds" value="<%= sp.permId %>" <%= sp.checked ? 'checked' : '' %> />
              <span class="permission-marker" aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
              <span class="permission-text"><%= sp.description || sp.label %></span>
            </label>
          <% }); %>
          <% if (itemIndex < section.items.length - 1) { %>
            <div class="permission-group-divider"></div>
          <% } %>
        <% }); %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% } %>
<% }); %>
